<!--
  The notification's small icon: `ld`, the same two letters as the launcher mark.

  It used to be `android.R.drawable.stat_sys_upload_done`, so on Android 12+ the status
  bar showed a generic upload glyph for a terminal session — one more system icon among
  system icons, and nothing that said which app was holding the connection.

  **Monochrome on purpose.** A notification small icon is drawn as an alpha mask and
  tinted by the system, so colour here is either discarded or printed as a solid block
  on some OEM skins. White fill, transparent background, 24 dp viewport, and no detail
  under two units: at 24 dp a stroke thinner than 2 vanishes.

  The letterforms are the launcher's geometry reduced to what survives at this size: two
  stems on one baseline with the `d`'s counter open enough to read as a letter rather
  than a bar. The launcher icon's chamfers and exact stroke weights are noise at 24 px
  and are not reproduced.

  CORRECTED 2026-11-06, on the operator's report that the stem of the `d` stood too far
  from its counter. Two changes, both measured against a render at 192 px and at 24 px:

  (1) The letters are 1 unit apart instead of 2. The gap was the largest empty run in the
      mark, so at 24 px the `l` read as a detached bar rather than the first letter of a
      pair.

  (2) The `d`'s bowl's right wall is the stem itself. Before, the bowl closed at x=16 and
      the stem occupied 16..18, so the right side of the `d` was 4 units of ink against 2
      on every other side, and the counter sat 2 units from the stem's edge. The counter
      now runs to the stem (11.5..15.5 against a stem at 15.5..17.5), which makes every
      stroke 2 units and puts the counter against the stem instead of across a gap from
      it.

  The ink is still centred exactly: it spans x 6.5..17.5, centre 12, on a 24 unit
  viewport, and every stroke is 2 units, which is the floor the comment below states.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="24dp"
    android:height="24dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">

    <!-- `l`: one stem, ascender to baseline. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M6.5,4h2v16h-2z" />

    <!-- `d`: the stem, then a bowl whose right wall is that stem. The counter is 4 units
         wide and ends where the stem begins, so the two sides of the letter weigh the
         same. -->
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:pathData="M15.5,4h2v16h-2z" />
    <path
        android:fillColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:fillType="evenOdd"
        android:pathData="M9.5,10h8v10h-8zM11.5,12h4v6h-4z" />
</vector>
